  "htmlPage": {
    "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/graph20/records/areas-of-effect/cone/"
  },
  "rulesText": "A Cone is an area of effect that extends in straight lines from a point of origin in a direction its creator chooses. A Cone's width at any point along its length is equal to that point's distance from the point of origin. For example, a Cone is 15 feet wide at a point along its length that is 15 feet from the point of origin. The effect that creates a Cone specifies its maximum length.\n\nA Cone's point of origin isn't included in the area of effect unless its creator decides otherwise."
}
